{"id":"mahabharata-12-010","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":10,"title":"दशमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 10 · Bhima's reply","summary":{"en":"Bhima says that Yudhishthira talks like a scholar who has lost his sense, and that action, not inaction, is the law of a man's life. He says that a king who gives up his duty is like a man who climbs a tree to take honey and does not eat.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಬುದ್ಧಿ ಕಳೆದುಕೊಂಡ ಪಂಡಿತನಂತೆ ಮಾತನಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಮನುಷ್ಯನ ಬಾಳಿನ ನಿಯಮ ಕ್ರಿಯೆಯೇ ಹೊರತು ನಿಷ್ಕ್ರಿಯತೆಯಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ಭೀಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕರ್ತವ್ಯ ತೊರೆದ ರಾಜ ಜೇನು ತೆಗೆಯಲು ಮರ ಹತ್ತಿ ತಿನ್ನದವನಂತೆ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीम कहते हैं कि युधिष्ठिर विवेक खो बैठे पण्डित की तरह बोल रहे हैं, और मनुष्य के जीवन का नियम कर्म है, अकर्म नहीं। वे कहते हैं कि कर्तव्य त्यागने वाला राजा उस व्यक्ति जैसा है जो मधु लेने पेड़ पर चढ़कर उसे खाता नहीं।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుడు వివేకం కోల్పోయిన పండితునిలా మాట్లాడుతున్నాడని, మనిషి జీవిత నియమం కర్మమే కానీ నిష్క్రియత కాదని భీముడు అంటాడు. కర్తవ్యం వదిలిన రాజు తేనె కోసం చెట్టెక్కి తినని వానిలాంటి వాడంటాడు.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரர் அறிவிழந்த பண்டிதன் போல் பேசுகிறார், மனிதரின் வாழ்க்கை விதி செயலே தவிர செயலின்மை அல்ல என்று பீமன் கூறுகிறான். கடமையை விட்ட மன்னன் தேனுக்கு மரமேறி உண்ணாதவன் போன்றவன் என்கிறான்.","ml":"യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ബുദ്ധിഭ്രമം വന്ന പണ്ഡിതനെപ്പോലെയാണ് സംസാരിക്കുന്നതെന്ന് ഭീമൻ പറയുന്നു; മനുഷ്യജീവിതത്തിന്റെ നിയമം പ്രവർത്തനമാണ്, നിഷ്ക്രിയതയല്ല. തേൻ എടുക്കാൻ മരത്തിൽ കയറിയിട്ട് തിന്നാതെ പോകുന്ന മനുഷ്യനെപ്പോലെയാണ് കടമ ഉപേക്ഷിക്കുന്ന രാജാവെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.10; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"भीम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhima said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"श्रोत्रियस्येव ते राजन्मन्दकस्याविपश्चितः ।\nअनुवाकहताबुद्धिर्नैषा तत्त्वार्थदर्शिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, your mind is like that of a dull, unlearned Vedic reciter, dulled by repeating the text. It does not see the real meaning."}},{"n":2,"text":"आलस्ये कृतचित्तस्य राजधर्मानसूयतः ।\nविनाशे धार्तराष्ट्राणां किं फलं भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one whose mind is set on idleness and who scorns the duties of a king, what was the use, best of the Bharatas, of destroying Dhritarashtra's sons?"}},{"n":3,"text":"क्षमानुकम्पा कारुण्यमानृशंस्यं न विद्यते ।\nक्षात्रमाचरतो मार्गमपि बन्धोस्त्वदन्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Forgiveness, pity, tenderness and gentleness do not exist for one who follows the warrior's path, not even toward a kinsman."}},{"n":4,"text":"यदीमां भवतो बुद्धिं विद्याम वयमीदृशीम् ।\nशस्त्रं नैव ग्रहीष्यामो न वधिष्याम कंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"If we had known that you would think in this way, we would never have taken up weapons nor killed anyone."}},{"n":5,"text":"भैक्ष्यमेवाचरिष्याम शरीरस्या विमोक्षणात् ।\nन चेदं दारुणं युद्धमभविष्यन्महीक्षिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We would simply have lived by begging until the release of the body, and this dreadful war of the kings would not have happened."}},{"n":6,"text":"प्राणस्यान्नमिदं सर्वमिति वै कवयो विदुः ।\nस्थावरं जङ्गमं चैव सर्वं प्राणस्य भोजनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise know that all this is food for life: whatever is moving or unmoving is the nourishment of life."}},{"n":7,"text":"आददानस्य चेद्राज्यं ये केचित्परिपन्थिनः ।\nहन्तव्यास्त इति प्राज्ञाः क्षत्रधर्मविदो विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who know the warrior's dharma, being wise, say that when someone is taking a kingdom, whoever stands in his way is to be killed."}},{"n":8,"text":"ते सदोषा हतास्माभी राज्यस्य परिपन्थिनः ।\nतान्हत्वा भुङ्क्ष्व धर्मेण युधिष्ठिर महीमिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those guilty enemies of the kingdom have been killed by us. Having killed them, Yudhishthira, enjoy this earth in accord with dharma."}},{"n":9,"text":"यथा हि पुरुषः खात्वा कूपमप्राप्य चोदकम् ।\nपङ्कदिग्धो निवर्तेत कर्मेदं नस्तथोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a man who digs a well and, finding no water, turns back smeared with mud, such is this deed of ours if we stop now."}},{"n":10,"text":"यथारुह्य महावृक्षमपहृत्य ततो मधु ।\nअप्राश्य निधनं गच्छेत्कर्मेदं नस्तथोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a man who climbs a great tree, takes the honey, and dies without tasting it, such is this deed of ours."}},{"n":11,"text":"यथा महान्तमध्वानमाशया पुरुषः पतन् ।\nस निराशो निवर्तेत कर्मेदं नस्तथोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a man who sets out on a long road in hope and then turns back in despair, such is this deed of ours."}},{"n":12,"text":"यथा शत्रून्घातयित्वा पुरुषः कुरुसत्तम ।\nआत्मानं घातयेत्पश्चात्कर्मेदं नस्तथाविधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a man, best of Kurus, who has had his enemies killed and afterwards kills himself, such is this deed of ours."}},{"n":13,"text":"यथान्नं क्षुधितो लब्ध्वा न भुञ्जीत यदृच्छया ।\nकामी च कामिनीं लब्ध्वा कर्मेदं नस्तथाविधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a hungry man who gets food and does not eat it, or a lover who wins his beloved and spurns her, such is this deed of ours."}},{"n":14,"text":"वयमेवात्र गर्ह्या हि ये वयं मन्दचेतसः ।\nत्वां राजन्ननुगच्छामो ज्येष्ठोऽयमिति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"We ourselves are to blame here, being slow of mind, for we follow you, king, thinking, \"He is the eldest.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"वयं हि बाहुबलिनः कृतविद्या मनस्विनः ।\nक्लीबस्य वाक्ये तिष्ठामो यथैवाशक्तयस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"We are strong in arm, learned and spirited, yet we stand by the word of a weakling, like men without power."}},{"n":16,"text":"अगतीन्कागतीनस्मान्नष्टार्थानर्थसिद्धये ।\nकथं वै नानुपश्येयुर्जनाः पश्यन्ति यादृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing us without recourse and our purposes ruined, how will people not judge us just as they now see us, when we are seeking our goals?"}},{"n":17,"text":"आपत्काले हि संन्यासः कर्तव्य इति शिष्यते ।\nजरयाभिपरीतेन शत्रुभिर्व्यंसितेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Renunciation is taught as a duty in times of calamity, when a man is overcome by old age or ruined by his enemies."}},{"n":18,"text":"तस्मादिह कृतप्रज्ञास्त्यागं न परिचक्षते ।\nधर्मव्यतिक्रमं चेदं मन्यन्ते सूक्ष्मदर्शिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore resolute men here do not commend renunciation, and the subtle thinkers regard it as a breach of dharma."}},{"n":19,"text":"कथं तस्मात्समुत्पन्नस्तन्निष्ठस्तदुपाश्रयः ।\nतदेव निन्दन्नासीत श्रद्धा वान्यत्र गृह्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can a man who has arisen from that order, rests in it and depends on it, stay there condemning it, or place his faith elsewhere?"}},{"n":20,"text":"श्रिया विहीनैरधनैर्नास्तिकैः संप्रवर्तितम् ।\nवेदवादस्य विज्ञानं सत्याभासमिवानृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The doctrine of Vedic statements spread by the wretched, the poor and the unbelievers is falsehood that merely looks like truth."}},{"n":21,"text":"शक्यं तु मौण्ड्यमास्थाय बिभ्रतात्मानमात्मना ।\nधर्मच्छद्म समास्थाय आसितुं न तु जीवितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One may take the shaven-headed state, supporting oneself by oneself, and sit idle under a cloak of dharma, but one cannot really live that way."}},{"n":22,"text":"शक्यं पुनररण्येषु सुखमेकेन जीवितुम् ।\nअबिभ्रता पुत्रपौत्रान्देवर्षीनतिथीन्पितॄन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One can live happily alone in forests, supporting no sons, grandsons, divine sages, guests or ancestors."}},{"n":23,"text":"नेमे मृगाः स्वर्गजितो न वराहा न पक्षिणः ।\nअथैतेन प्रकारेण पुण्यमाहुर्न ताञ्जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These deer, boars and birds are not conquerors of heaven, and people do not call them meritorious by this reasoning."}},{"n":24,"text":"यदि संन्यासतः सिद्धिं राजन्कश्चिदवाप्नुयात् ।\nपर्वताश्च द्रुमाश्चैव क्षिप्रं सिद्धिमवाप्नुयुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, O king, anyone could win success by renunciation, mountains and trees would quickly win it."}},{"n":25,"text":"एते हि नित्यसंन्यासा दृश्यन्ते निरुपद्रवाः ।\nअपरिग्रहवन्तश्च सततं चात्मचारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For these are seen as constantly renouncing, undisturbed, owning nothing and always living in themselves."}},{"n":26,"text":"अथ चेदात्मभाग्येषु नान्येषां सिद्धिमश्नुते ।\nतस्मात्कर्मैव कर्तव्यं नास्ति सिद्धिरकर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But if success comes through one's own share and not through others', then action alone should be done; there is no success without action."}},{"n":27,"text":"औदकाः सृष्टयश्चैव जन्तवः सिद्धिमाप्नुयुः ।\nयेषामात्मैव भर्तव्यो नान्यः कश्चन विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even water creatures and the beings of creation attain success, for each must support only itself, and no one else."}},{"n":28,"text":"अवेक्षस्व यथा स्वैः स्वैः कर्मभिर्व्यापृतं जगत् ।\nतस्मात्कर्मैव कर्तव्यं नास्ति सिद्धिरकर्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look at how the world is busy with its own deeds. Therefore action alone should be done; there is no success without action."}}]}]}